.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt FSCK_EXFAT 8
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm fsck_exfat
.Nd exFAT file system consistency check
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl q
.Ar special
.Nm
.Op Fl fnpy
.Ar special
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
checks an exFAT file system:
its boot region (signatures, geometry and checksum, against its backup),
its system files (the allocation bitmap, and the up-case table and its
checksum), every directory's entry sets (their checksums and name
hashes, and their cluster chains: valid, without loops and not shared
with another file), and the bitmap against the clusters in use.
.Pp
It repairs a damaged main boot region from its backup, the bitmap,
entry set checksums and name hashes, and clears the volume's dirty flag
once nothing is left to repair.
With a broken chain or directory, it leaves the bitmap as it is: what
those held would look free and be given away.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl q
Only tells whether the volume was unmounted cleanly, from its dirty
flag: the exit status is 0 when it was, 3 when not.
.Xr diskarbitrationd 8
asks this before mounting an exFAT volume.
.It Fl n
Makes no change, and answers no to every question.
.It Fl y
Repairs without asking.
.It Fl p
Preens: checks a volume only if it is dirty (or with
.Fl f ) ,
and repairs without asking.
.It Fl f
With
.Fl p ,
checks a clean volume as well.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the volume is fine or was repaired; 3 with
.Fl q
when it is dirty; 8 when problems are left.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr newfs_exfat 8 ,
.Xr fsck 8
.Sh STANDARDS
Microsoft's exFAT file system specification.
.Sh HISTORY
This
.Nm
was written for Minkar.
